    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200256424822_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor-Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2022-02-08\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nAdjunct Instructor – Liberal Arts Chemistry Lab Huntington University seeks to fill an adjunct teaching position in chemistry.  The qualified candidate will be asked to teach two or three sections of CH111L, Lab for Chemistry in Contemporary Society, per semester. Each lab section meets for one 2-hour time block per week. Evening hours are available if needed.    Qualifications Master’s degree in a chemistry or biology-related field, or 5 years of relevant laboratory experience Demonstrated potential for college-level teaching  Familiarity with lab safety protocol and lab teaching logistics Supportive of a Christian faith environment and the University’s educational goals  Should enjoy creatively and interactively teaching non-science majors General Information:   Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university.  Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals.   Statement of Faith Work Schedule:  This is a part-time, exempt position.  To Apply:   Apply via ADP and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Jean Cole, Human Resources Manager.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200254409679_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Bus Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2022-02-02\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University seeks part-time bus drivers for a 35 passenger bus.  The Bus Driver is responsible for transporting students, staff, coaches, and passengers safely to and from their destination in the established times and in all types of weather and road conditions, observing legal, safe, and defensive driving practices.  QUALIFICATIONS:   Must have a strong personal faith in Jesus Christ, a desire to serve others and a commitment to being a faithful steward of university resources Must have a “clean” driving record Have sufficient physical and mental abilities to operate a school bus/van in a safe manner Must be narcotic drug and alcohol free Professional driving experience preferred This is a part-time, on call position Must possess a valid commercial driver’s with passenger endorsement Minimum age of 25 years  RESPONSIBILITIES:   Bus/Van Maintain vehicle by conducting safety inspection, inspect the interior and exterior and the engine prior to use Maintain order among passengers and report any behavioral issues to the appropriate personnel, assure passengers understand bus rules of safety Assist students, staff, coaches, and passengers in and out of vehicle as needed Assist students, staff, coaches, and passengers with loading and unloading equipment as needed   Administrative   Collaborate with coaching and administrative staff to establish transportation schedule Maintain and update route sheets and schedules, manifesto along with emergency contact information Assist with other projects and perform other duties as assigned by the VP of Business & Finance Treasurer  Physical Requirements of the Position:   Employee is regularly required to focus, see, speak, and hear and to have dexterity of the hands and fingers Must be able to sit for extended periods of time while driving Other duties may require bending, kneeling, twisting, and reaching overhead, above shoulders and horizontally May be required to lift, carry, and/or push moderately heavy persons in effort to evacuate the bus/van in case of emergency Shall be required to meet all regulatory standards as directed by the State of Indiana as a driver General Information:   Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university.  Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals.   Statement of Faith Work Schedule:  This is a part-time, non-exempt position.  The driving schedule varies depending on scheduling and workflow demands. To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
